Concrete execution exposed a real semantic bug in the `reverse=True` branch: it reversed the source list before sorting instead of reversing the ascending sort. I’ve isolated that rule and am correcting it before writing any proof claims; this is exactly why the `krun` gate precedes `kprove`.
